<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wu Guang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 208 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guan-people">Guang</a> was, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chen-sheng">Chen Sheng</a>, a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dazexiang-uprising">Dazexiang uprising</a> of 209 BCE, the first great peasant rising in Chinese history. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conscription">Conscripts</a> held up by rain and facing death for lateness, they rebelled and founded the Zhangchu regime, which set the Qin empire ablaze; Wu Guang was killed by his own officers the next year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wu-guang.jpg" alt="Wu Guang" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Qin_Uprisings.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
